# Cloudflare Pages headers — Boss Demo V1 preview.
#
# X-Robots-Tag is the transport-level counterpart to the meta robots tag. It
# still applies to responses a crawler fetches directly (assets, a URL reached
# without reading robots.txt first), which the HTML meta tag cannot cover.
#
# The directive list matches DRAFT_ROBOTS in src/data/blog/visibility.ts. The
# private demo serves draft articles and real product screenshots, so the two
# extra directives are load-bearing: `nosnippet` stops draft copy appearing in
# a result even when the page itself is never indexed, and `noimageindex` keeps
# the masked product screenshots out of image search. An image reached directly
# never parses the HTML meta tag, so this header is the only thing covering it.
#
# AT GO-LIVE: remove the X-Robots-Tag block below together with the
# public/robots.txt change and VITE_ALLOW_INDEXING=true. See
# docs/LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.md.

/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive, nosnippet, noimageindex
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
